{
    "name": "Wien-Bridge Sine Oscillator (16 Hz)",
    "description": "A classic Wien-bridge sine-wave oscillator: an op-amp non-inverting amplifier (gain ~3.2) closed around a Wien RC network (R=10k, C=1uF, f0 = 1/2πRC ≈ 16 Hz), with anti-parallel diode pairs softly limiting the gain for amplitude stabilization. IMPORTANT: a symmetric oscillator sits at a perfect equilibrium in simulation — run the included analysisConfig (transient with an initialConditions seed on the np node) and it self-starts into a sustained ±1.72V sine at ~15.8 Hz, stable to 5 significant figures. (Validated on ngspice.)",
    "tags": ["oscillator", "wien-bridge", "sine", "opamp", "analog", "advanced"],
    "analysisConfig": {
        "analysis": {
            "type": "tran",
            "stopTime": "0.8",
            "stepTime": "50u",
            "initialConditions": {
                "np": 0.5
            }
        },
        "probes": ["v(out)", "v(np)"]
    },
